Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@, python3, systemd
Recommends: kitty
Conflicts: audacious, audacious-plugins, audacious-plugins-data
Replaces: audacious, audacious-plugins, audacious-plugins-data
Provides: audacious
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/erikvanhamme/audacious
Description: Audacious audio player with a terminal interface
 Audacious plays music in a terminal: a notcurses interface with the
 controls and progress, the playlist and the song that plays. It plays FLAC,
 MP3 and WAV with ReplayGain over PipeWire, and can be controlled with
 playerctl over MPRIS and with audtool. It is built for a small footprint:
 without GTK, Qt or any other graphical library.
 .
 audacious starts in the terminal it is run in. Run without one, as from the
 application launcher, it starts in a kitty window when kitty is installed,
 or hands the files to the audacious that already runs.
 .
 This package holds audacious and audacious-plugins @UPSTREAM_VERSION@ with
 the terminal interface of HyprDebian, built from @SOURCE@ of the forks. It
 replaces the packages audacious and audacious-plugins of Debian.
